---
import { site } from "../data/site";
import ArticleLayout from "../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout
	description="The software, fonts, original media, and upstream notices behind this website."
	eyebrow="PROJECT / LICENSES"
	title="Licenses & attribution"
>
	<h2>SolidCraft</h2>
	<p>
		SolidCraft is licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option. Read the
		<a href="/notices/SolidCraft-MIT.txt">MIT license</a>
		,
		<a href="/notices/SolidCraft-Apache-2.0.txt">Apache-2.0 license</a>
		, and
		<a href="/notices/SolidCraft-ATTRIBUTION.md">asset attribution inventory</a>
		from the pinned source used here.
	</p>
	<h2 id="solidcore">SolidCore</h2>
	<p>
		SolidCore is an independent Rust port of NVIDIA’s SMLib from USD BRep. It is
		licensed under Apache-2.0 and retains upstream notices. Read its
		<a href="/notices/SolidCore-LICENSE.txt">license</a>
		,
		<a href="/notices/SolidCore-NOTICE.txt">NOTICE</a>
		, and
		<a href="/notices/SolidCore-ATTRIBUTION.md">attribution</a>
		.
	</p>
	<p>
		NVIDIA and SMLib identify the upstream source. They do not imply affiliation
		or endorsement.
	</p>
	<h2>Website code</h2>
	<p>
		This repository’s existing<a href="/notices/Website-MIT.txt">
			MIT license
		</a> covers its website code. Third-party software, fonts, and reused
		project media retain their own terms.
	</p>
	<h2>Typography</h2>
	<p>
		IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono are self-hosted through pinned Fontsource
		distributions. Both use the SIL Open Font License. Their notices are
		included here:
		<a href="/notices/IBM-Plex-Sans-OFL.txt">Sans OFL</a>
		and
		<a href="/notices/IBM-Plex-Mono-OFL.txt">Mono OFL</a>
		.
	</p>
	<h2>Original product media & branding</h2>
	<p>
		The SolidCraft mark, supplied social banner, sample plate, and enclosure
		recording are original upstream assets by SolidCraft contributors. Their
		attribution lists MIT OR Apache-2.0. Video posters are unretouched frames
		extracted from those recordings.
	</p>
	<p>
		The SELENE rover model is by
		<a href="https://github.com/0xlillith/solidcraft-rover">0xlillith</a>
		; the recording is by SolidCraft contributors. See the creator’s source
		repository for model-specific terms and Ubuntu Light lettering notices. See
		the<a href="/showcase/selene/">showcase notes</a> and upstream attribution
		for recording provenance.
	</p>
	<p>
		The B-rep illustration is an original SVG created for this website. Menu and
		action icons use Lucide; its<a href="/notices/Lucide-LICENSE.txt">
			ISC license and Feather notices
		</a> are included. Other interface icons are small original SVG paths. No
		proprietary CAD screenshots or third-party product icons are used.
	</p>
	<h2>Dependencies & source records</h2>
	<p>
		Zustand manages shared interface state under its
		<a href="/notices/Zustand-LICENSE.txt">MIT license</a>
		. Live progress reports are sanitized with DOMPurify; its<a
			href="/notices/DOMPurify-LICENSE.txt"
		>
			license terms
		</a> are included.
	</p>
	<p>
		Exact application and build-tool versions are recorded in<code>
			package.json
		</code> and
		<code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code>
		. The checked-in source and media manifests record upstream revisions and
		asset digests. The<a href={site.repo}>SolidCraft</a> and
		<a href={site.kernel}>SolidCore</a>
		repositories remain the authorities for their own distributions.
	</p>
</ArticleLayout>
